# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres (self-hosted: PostgreSQL 17 + TimescaleDB)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both strings point at the SAME database. Historically they differed (a pooled
# vs a direct endpoint on the old managed host); the self-hosted VPS has no
# pooler, so locally and in production the two are identical. The split is kept
# because the code still reads both:
#
#   DATABASE_URL         The web app and the worker's normal query path.
#   DATABASE_URL_DIRECT  Anything that needs session state: drizzle-kit
#                        migrations, `drizzle-kit studio`, COPY, CREATE EXTENSION,
#                        advisory locks. Must be a DIRECT (non-pooled) connection;
#                        migrations refuse a pooled one.
#
# On the VPS both point at localhost:5432 (no SSL over the loopback). For local
# development against the VPS database, tunnel it over SSH and point both here at
# the forwarded port. See docs/operations/deployment.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://equitywise:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/nse_signals"
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT="postgresql://equitywise:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/nse_signals"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration tests (local, disposable database)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The DB-backed suites run against a THROWAWAY local database, never a real one.
# `pnpm test:integration` starts docker-compose.test.yml (Postgres 17 +
# TimescaleDB, matching the VPS), migrates it, runs the suite, and tears it down
# — you do not need to set anything for that.
#
# Set this only to point Vitest at a test database you manage yourself (e.g. for
# `pnpm test:watch`). It MUST be local and its name MUST end in `_test`, or the
# suites refuse to run — a guard so a test can never touch a real database.
# Leave it blank and the DB suites skip locally (they are REQUIRED in CI).
TEST_DATABASE_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Market data — which provider serves the app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `fyers` (default — unset behaves exactly as before this switch existed),
# `dhan`, or `routed`. Both the web app and the worker read it. A provider must
# have its identity configured below (FYERS_APP_ID / DHAN_CLIENT_ID) to be
# selectable; naming one that is not is a startup error with a remedy, not a
# quiet outage. `routed` needs both.
#
# The worker BUILDS every provider whose identity is set and keeps each of
# their tokens fresh in `provider_credentials` (one row per provider), so a
# switch is this one line plus a restart of both processes — no re-login.
# Rows written by one provider are tagged with its id (`provider_id` on
# candles/instruments), so history from either source stays attributable.
MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER="fyers"

# `routed` sends each question to the provider best at it and asks the other
# when that one fails (auth / rate limit / upstream — never for "not found").
# Defaults are the production split (docs/planning/dhan-provider-plan.md §5,
# amended by §10f); override any route with `fyers` or `dhan`:
#
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_BARS            daily & weekly history      default dhan
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_INTRADAY_BARS   1m–1h history               default fyers
#                                     (Dhan's equity 1m ends at 15:14 — verified)
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_QUOTES          snapshot quotes             default dhan
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_INSTRUMENTS     instrument master           default dhan
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_STATUS          market open/closed          default fyers
#                                     (Dhan has no status endpoint)
#   MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_STREAM          live tick socket            default fyers
#                                     (Dhan's socket is built and live-verified;
#                                     5,000 symbols/connection vs Fyers' 200 —
#                                     set `dhan` when the 200 cap binds)
#   MARKET_DATA_FALLBACK              0 disables the second opinion (measurement)
#
# Leave them unset for the defaults. `/data-sources` shows the live table.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fyers API v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create an app at https://fyers.in/web/api-dashboard/user-apps
#   - Redirect URI must match FYERS_REDIRECT_URI below exactly.
#   - "Market Data" permission is required for history and quotes.
#   - Since 1 Apr 2026 SEBI requires a separate, IP-whitelisted app for ORDER
#     placement. A data-only app needs no static IP.
FYERS_APP_ID=""            # e.g. SPXXXXE7-100
FYERS_SECRET_KEY=""        # app secret; never commit
FYERS_REDIRECT_URI="https://trade.fyers.in/api-login/redirect-uri/index.html"

# Access token. Expires daily — the refresh-token flow was discontinued on
# 1 Apr 2026 and daily 2FA is now mandatory.
#
# A FALLBACK, not the normal path. When the three fields below are set, the
# worker mints a token every morning and stores it in the `provider_credentials`
# table, and both the worker and the web app read it from there. This value is
# used only when no stored credential is usable — a fresh checkout, or a
# deliberate choice to log in by hand (`pnpm fyers:login`).
FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# Live tick socket for the watchlist (web app only). Set to 0 to disable; the
# watchlist then falls back to a 3-second server-side poll. See
# docs/operations/deployment.md §5 "Live prices".
FYERS_STREAM=1

# Unattended daily re-login. Set all three and the token refreshes on its own at
# 08:30 IST; leave all three blank to log in by hand every day. Setting only
# some of them is an error the worker reports at startup rather than a partial
# configuration that silently never refreshes.
#
# Uses UNDOCUMENTED Fyers endpoints that may break without notice; a failure is
# logged loudly and asks you to log in by hand rather than retrying blindly.
#
# THESE ARE ACCOUNT-LEVEL SECRETS. FYERS_TOTP_SECRET is the same 2FA seed that
# protects your brokerage login, including the order-placing side this app
# deliberately has nothing to do with. Give them ONLY to the worker, on a host
# you control. Never put them on a serverless deploy: a deployed web app needs
# the minted token and nothing more, and that token dies within the day and can
# only read market data.
FYERS_ID=""                # your FYERS login ID, e.g. XK12345
FYERS_TOTP_SECRET=""       # base32 secret from 2FA setup
FYERS_PIN=""               # 4-digit login PIN

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dhan (DhanHQ API v2) — second market-data provider
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Status: Phases 0–4 done (docs/planning/dhan-provider-plan.md). The worker
# mints a Dhan token from these at 01:35 IST daily and at startup, stores it in
# `provider_credentials` under `dhan`, and the web app reads it from there —
# the same split as Fyers. `pnpm dhan:probe` still proves the account end to
# end before the first run.
#
# What you need on the Dhan side, once:
#   1. Data API subscription — web.dhan.co → DhanHQ Trading APIs → Data APIs.
#      ₹499 + GST per 30 days, auto-debited from the trading balance. Without
#      it, quotes/history/socket return an authorisation error.
#   2. TOTP enabled on the account (Dhan app → Profile → Security → 2FA /
#      authenticator). Copy the base32 SETUP KEY shown alongside the QR code,
#      not a 6-digit code — the worker generates codes from the seed.
#   3. Your client ID (the 10-digit number on your profile) and login PIN.
#
# No API key/secret and no static IP are needed: those exist only for ORDER
# APIs, which this app never calls. Dhan's TOTP mint is a DOCUMENTED endpoint
# (unlike Fyers'); a token lives 24 h from its mint and can be minted at most
# once every 2 minutes. `RenewToken` does not apply to TOTP-minted tokens
# (verified), so the worker simply re-mints nightly.
#
# THESE ARE ACCOUNT-LEVEL SECRETS, exactly like FYERS_TOTP_SECRET above: they
# belong to the worker and a developer machine only, never to the web app.
DHAN_CLIENT_ID=""          # 10-digit client id, e.g. 1000000001
DHAN_PIN=""                # login PIN
DHAN_TOTP_SECRET=""        # base32 setup key from the authenticator enrolment

# Optional: a token minted elsewhere (web.dhan.co → Access Token, 24 h). The
# same FALLBACK as FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN: used only when no stored credential is
# usable. Left blank in normal operation.
DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# Live tick socket over Dhan's documented binary feed (web app only; needs no
# SDK). Set to 0 to disable, like FYERS_STREAM. Only used when the stream
# route points at Dhan (MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=dhan, or routed with
# MARKET_DATA_ROUTE_STREAM=dhan).
DHAN_STREAM=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (first-party, multi-user — docs/planning/authentication-plan.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   AUTH_SESSION_SECRET   32+ random bytes; signs the session cookie. REQUIRED in prod.
#   AUTH_ALLOW_SIGNUP     "false" closes public sign-up. Default: open.
#   AUTH_BASE_URL         base URL used in email links. Default: https://equitywise.io (prod).
#
# Transactional email (verification + password reset) via Resend. With no key,
# links are printed to the server log — fine for local dev.
#   RESEND_API_KEY        Resend API key (re_...). REQUIRED for real email delivery.
#   AUTH_EMAIL_FROM       Sender. Default: "EquityWise Support <support@equitywise.io>".
#                         Must be an address on the Resend-verified domain.
#   AVATAR_UPLOAD_DIR     Where profile avatars are written. Default: <cwd>/uploads/avatars.
#                         In prod, point this at a persistent dir Nginx can also serve.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=""
AUTH_ALLOW_SIGNUP="true"
RESEND_API_KEY=""
AUTH_EMAIL_FROM="EquityWise Support <support@equitywise.io>"
AVATAR_UPLOAD_DIR=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploying on the VPS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE IS NOT DEPLOYED. `.env` is gitignored. On the VPS the real .env
# lives outside the git checkout, root-owned and `chmod 600`; `next.config.ts`
# dotenv-loads the repo-root path. Both processes run under PM2 (see the
# Production Hosting & VPS Migration Plan for the full runbook).
#
# The web app (apps/web) needs these values, and no secret beyond them:
#
#   DATABASE_URL                        the POOLED database string
#   MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER                which provider serves pages (optional)
#   FYERS_APP_ID                        Fyers identity — live-quote routes only
#   DHAN_CLIENT_ID                      Dhan identity — only if Dhan is selected
#
# FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN / DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN are NOT in that list, and deliberately
# so. The worker mints a token each day into `provider_credentials`; the web
# app reads it from there. DHAN_PIN and DHAN_TOTP_SECRET never go on the web host.
#
# `next build` does NOT fail when the Clerk keys are absent. `clerkMiddleware`
# throws instead, on every request, so the whole site answers 500 — /sign-in
# included, because the middleware runs before it. That is the error you are
# reading if a running app serves nothing.
#
# Keep the web app's environment to those values. DATABASE_URL_DIRECT,
# FYERS_SECRET_KEY, FYERS_ID, FYERS_TOTP_SECRET and FYERS_PIN belong ONLY to the
# worker (and a developer machine): migrations, the OAuth handshake and the daily
# re-login run there. An unused secret is still a secret at risk, and the TOTP
# seed and PIN are account-level — see the Fyers section above.
#
#   - /api/fyers/connect and /callback (the Fyers OAuth handshake) write the new token into
#     .fyers-token.json and this repo's .env — which the VPS filesystem allows.
#     With the worker's daily refresh running, nothing here needs doing at all.
#   - apps/worker runs under PM2 on the same VPS. It is what writes new candles,
#     signals and paper trades and refreshes the token; without it the site
#     serves whatever it last stored.
